  "notes": [
   "Catalogue breadboard banks: the image's top half (rows f-j) is bank 'b' and its bottom half (rows a-e) is bank 't'; port names follow the catalogue.",
   "Resistors bridge the centre gap: leg 1 in row f (bank b), leg 2 in row e (bank t), in the same column as the LED anode.",
   "LED anodes (bent, longer leg) are in columns 7,10,13,16,19,22 and cathodes in the next column; each cathode goes via a short black jumper from row i to the top negative rail (tn).",
   "Exact rail hole numbers (tn.N) are approximate; the whole rail is one strip so connectivity is unaffected.",
   "Arduino GND next to AREF is mapped to uno GND.1; the ground wire goes to the top negative rail.",
   "Resistor value 220 ohm per the tutorial text and schematic; the first LED is on pin 7 and the last on pin 2 per the image."
  ]
 },
